    "body": "## Summary\n- enforce the existing symmetric user-block policy when a worker accepts an open job\n- reject blocked relationships before assignment, live-tracking initialization or acceptance notification\n- keep the rejection neutral so the API does not reveal which side created the block\n- preserve existing active-job lifecycle semantics; creating a block does not silently cancel escrow-backed work already in progress\n- add a regression test proving blocked acceptance has no persistence/tracking/notification side effects\n- document the new enforcement boundary\n\n## Safety / privacy\n- reverse-block state remains private\n- no new exact-location, route, live-tracking, escrow, payment or moderation data is exposed\n- active jobs are not mutated by blocking; dedicated completion/dispute/location authorization remains authoritative\n\n## Validation\nRun Maven verify, frontend lint/build and the repository's existing runtime/smoke workflows. Do not merge unless required checks are green.",
